ations, against 6 for sites with fewer. That is 16 times more."}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":"17 of the 200 sites had zero AI citations, and small sites were the most likely to have none: 67% of sites with under 50 visible pages had zero."}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":["Source: ",["$","a","a-0",{"href":"https://www.outrank.so/case-studies/how-to-get-cited-by-chatgpt","children":"https://www.outrank.so/case-studies/how-to-get-cited-by-chatgpt"}]]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p","p-9",{"children":"The practical reading is that Google visibility and third-party links come first, and AI citations tend to follow. Outrank is built around that sequence. It does not claim a guaranteed citation from any specific assistant."}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"id":"how-outrank-produces-content","children":"How Outrank produces content"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-5",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":"Research: for each article Outrank runs several fact-finding queries that return source URLs, searches Google for existing pages on the keyword, and reads the most relevant competing pages in full. Facts keep their source links so the writer can cite them."}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":"Planning: a strategist step chooses the structure, internal links and, when it adds value, a FAQ section of 3 to 4 questions placed last."}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":"Writing and review: one model family writes the article and a different model family reviews it. The review has a pass threshold, can trigger one revision round, and checks for generic phrasing."}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":"Link and date checks: outbound links are checked to confirm they load, and dates are checked against the current date. This is a link and date check, not a claim-by-claim verification against each source. Customers who need human fact-checking can add the Human Curated Service."}],"\n",["$","li","li-4",{"children":"Images: up to 4 images per article (5 with Premium Images)."}],"\n",["$","li","li-5",{"children":"Internal links: added from the customer's sitemap when one is available."}],"\n",["$","li","li-6",{"children":"Formats: guides (how-to, explainer, comparison, reference) and listicles (roundups, resources, examples), from about 1,200 to 4,200 words depending on the chosen length."}],"\n",["$","li","li-7",{"children":"Languages: more than 150 languages."}],"\n",["$","li","li-8",{"children":"Publishing: WordPress, WordPress.com, Webflow, Shopify, Wix, Framer, Notion, Ghost, Next.js blog, or any system through a custom webhook, as live posts or drafts, on days the customer chooses."}],"\n",["$","li","li-9",{"children":"Limit: articles are markdown published through the customer's CMS. Outrank does not add structured data markup to customer articles, so schema depends on the CMS or theme."}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"id":"how-outrank-builds-backlinks","children":"How Outrank builds backlinks"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-6",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":"Included exchange: customers host links to other Outrank customers inside their own articles and earn credits when a hosted link is verified. Credits earned depend on the hosting site's Domain Rating, capped at 20 per link. Hosting sites need a Domain Rating of at least 5, blog-hosting platforms such as wordpress.com, Medium and Substack are excluded, and an article carries at most 2 backlinks (3 for trusted hosts). Matching uses topical relevance and language, with cooldowns to prevent reciprocal and repeat linking."}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":"Verification: a scheduled job re-checks each placement and tracks it as created, not verified or lost."}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":"Marketplace placements (paid backlink plans): a 250 to 350 word section about the customer's site is placed inside an article on a blog with Domain Rating 30 or higher and at least 100 organic Google clicks per month. Links are monitored for 90 days with a 7-day recovery window, and the verifier detects nofollow, sponsored and ugc link attributes. Seller sites are scanned for inappropriate content."}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":["Network data (October 13, 2026): 530,154 backlinks verified live on host pages across the exchange and marketplace. Between September 13 and October 12, 2026, sites that let their own articles host links received a median of 21 verified backlinks, against 6 for sites that did not. Half of the sites that signed up between June and August 2026 and connected a blog had their first verified backlink within 3.8 days. Method and downloadable data: ",["$","a","a-0",{"href":"https://www.outrank.so/blog/how-to-generate-backlinks-automatically","children":"https://www.outrank.so/blog/how-to-generate-backlinks-automatically"}]]}],"\n",["$","li","li-4",{"children":"Limit: these are exchange and marketplace placements, not editorial press coverage or digital PR."}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"id":"how-outrank-keeps-pages-working","children":"How Outrank keeps pages working"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-7",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":"The improvements feature reads Google Search Console data and finds pages with at least 500 impressions and an average position between 4 and 25 that have room to gain clicks. It then drafts a rewrite using current search results, fresh facts and the customer's backlink targets."}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":"The rewrite checks for answer-ready FAQ sections and outbound citations, which help pages qualify for AI Overviews."}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":"By default Outrank hands the rewrite to the customer for approval. Automatic pushing to the website is off unless the customer enables it."}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":["Docs: ",["$","a","a-0",{"href":"https://www.outrank.so/docs/improvements","children":"https://www.outrank.so/docs/improvements"}]]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"id":"product-overview","children":"Product overview"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-8",{"children":["\n",